passage('G1.positive-kernel-integrals','supplement',[722,748],['S8','S9'],'Positive-interval integrability and exact antiderivatives justify both crossing integrations.',['cap_inv_sqrt_intervalIntegrable','cap_inv_mul_sqrt_intervalIntegrable','cap_integral_inv_sqrt','cap_integral_inv_mul_sqrt','cap_const_inv_continuousOn','cap_const_inv_sqrt_continuousOn','cap_const_inv_mul_sqrt_continuousOn','cap_integral_const_inv','cap_integral_const_inv_sqrt','cap_integral_const_inv_mul_sqrt'],'On positive intervals all denominators are nonzero. The exact integrals are A*log(b/a),2A*(sqrt b-sqrt a), and2A/sqrt a-2A/sqrt b. Genuine continuous-function interval integrability is supplied before using their integrals.','Supporting scalar calculus for the exact normalized endpoint; no analytic remainder input.')
